  "entry": "code/README.md",
  "notes": "Found in a public repository and run by a computer-use agent (batch public-1). Painting a desired recording-density pattern (a 'blueprint') onto a Neuropixels probe's electrodes and having the app build a channel map (.imro) that respects the probe's shared-channel hardware limits, while channel efficiency and density plots show how well the map matches the blueprint. Data used in the run: synthetic. tree.json is the workflow the agent did and a second agent replayed; run.json says how.",
